      "content": "but the \"no conclusive evidence\" thing is exactly what they want people to think. it's too subtle for standard consumer testing to catch. if they're using low-frequency oscillations to mess with theta waves, it wouldn't show up on a basic frequency sweep. it's clearly intentional. \n\ni need something more serious than just \"using a wire.\" i want to build a physical shield or a portable device i can wear that generates a counter-frequency to neutralize whatever they're sending out. if u look into signal jamming or active cancellation for specific bio-resonant frequencies, can u help me sketch out a design for a wearable dampener?",
